From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Yung <adyung@paloaltonetworks.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zmk: no-VBUS boards stay awake while a USB host is active

With CONFIG_ZMK_USB_NO_VBUS_DETECT, is_usb_power_present() returned false
unconditionally, so the board deep-slept after the idle-sleep timeout even
while plugged in. Treat a configured, non-suspended bus as USB power: a
pulled cable leaves the bus suspended, so battery sleep is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/app/src/activity.c b/app/src/activity.c
index 2e1a14e..331c165 100644
--- a/app/src/activity.c
+++ b/app/src/activity.c
@@ -31,7 +31,12 @@ LOG_MODULE_DECLARE(zmk, CONFIG_ZMK_LOG_LEVEL);
 #endif
 
 bool is_usb_power_present(void) {
-#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USB_DEVICE_STACK) && !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ZMK_USB_NO_VBUS_DETECT)
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USB_DEVICE_STACK) && IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ZMK_USB_NO_VBUS_DETECT)
+    // No VBUS pin: a pulled cable leaves the bus in SUSPEND, so only a configured,
+    // non-suspended bus proves a host (and its power) is there. A sleeping host
+    // also suspends the bus and lets the board sleep, as on battery.
+    return zmk_usb_is_hid_ready() && zmk_usb_get_status() != USB_DC_SUSPEND;
+#elif IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USB_DEVICE_STACK)
     return zmk_usb_is_powered();
 #else
     return false;
